From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:59:32 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: keep the silicon workarounds on Apple7 and
 Apple8

The block that retires workarounds on macOS 27 clears the whole first
seven, so an Apple7 or Apple8 GPU lost them as soon as the operating
system was new enough. Two of them work around defects in the silicon,
which no operating system release can retire there.

KK_WORKAROUND_4 replaces simd_is_helper_thread() with a variable the shader
updates at every demote, because the Metal query does not observe a
discard_fragment() that ran before it. The workaround's own documentation
records the defect as present in M1 and M2 chips. Without it the compiler
folds the repeated queries of
dEQP-VK.draw.renderpass.shader_invocation.helper_invocation and its
volatile variants into one: the read that precedes a demote reports the
state that follows it, and the quad broadcasts the test builds from the
helper value come out wrong.

KK_WORKAROUND_3 routes every ballot and vote through simd_or, because
Metal's simd_ballot, quad_any and quad_all answer for every thread the SIMD
group entered the shader with rather than the threads active where the
call sits. Its entry already names the test that then fails:
dEQP-VK.subgroups.shader_quad_control.divergent_condition puts
subgroupQuadAny and subgroupQuadAll inside a condition that only part of
each 2x2 quad satisfies, and on an Apple7 GPU under macOS 27.0 (build
26A428) the native quad votes answer for the whole quad instead, so the
green channel comes out set where the test requires it clear. The same
entry lists dEQP-VK.subgroups.ballot_other.*.subgroupballotfindlsb and
dEQP-VK.subgroups.arithmetic.graphics.* for the simd_ballot form of the
defect.

Keep both workarounds on Apple family eight and below and retire the rest
as before. The new kosmickrisp_helper_invocation_demote test renders the
helper-invocation conformance shape - one fully covered quad whose
invocations demote around an atomic - on an unclipped triangle scissored
to that quad, so the expected colour is exact; it reads 1/4881/4881/8881
without the workaround and 1/4321/4881/8881 with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
